ersistent effect's Potency and other secondary spell factors determined? Does the item need to be &quot;initialized&quot; after the Imbument process?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T11:35:08-07:00","id":1319545,"title":"","content":"Got my copy downloaded safely.<br /> <br /> ...incidentally, I do not see a link to a Google Form errata page anywhere in either its DRPG page or on its page on the OPP site. Where's it at?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T11:45:05-07:00","id":1319547,"title":"","content":"Just got mine downloaded. First thing I have noticed is that the chapter page number for chapter 6 appears to be incorrect. It says 122 which is before the previous chapter ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12789-psudonym55","name":"psudonym55","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T12:26:51-07:00","id":1319553,"title":"","content":"On page 34 in the Aedes vs. Supernal Phenomena, it says &quot;on p. XX&quot;. I think someone forgot to fill in the page number. Hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","user":"RobinCoyote","date":". 06-20-2019, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25329-robincoyote","name":"RobinCoyote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T12:28:54-07:00","id":1319554,"title":"","content":"No, we don\u2019t do those until after the errata phase any more, in case something caught in the form fucks with pagination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T12:43:12-07:00","id":1319557,"title":"","content":"In the full-size preview on DTRPG there is no heading for Chapter 3 in the ToC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 06-19-2019, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T13:31:18-07:00","id":1319564,"title":"","content":"It says the Raptor is served by the Sycorian Ministry. I initially thought that was referencing Sycorax, but that might be Sycoraxian? And a search found that Sycorian is a thing (pre-arranged marriages? maybe Syrian? search results keep pushing me towards Indian/Syrian webpages), but I couldn't find a definition, does anyone know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-19-2019, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T13:51:56-07:00","id":1319569,"title":"","content":"Where is errata being collected? I don't see the usual thread.<br /> <br /> I don't even know if this counts as errata anyway - the Dice Pool for the Clash of Wills initiated by Piercing Glance is undefined - Peripheral Mage Sight isn't tied to a specific Arcanum, as far as I know, so which one to add to Gnosis is unclear. I assume it'd be the highest, but it'd be nice if that was clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T13:56:23-07:00","id":1319570,"title":"","content":"There <i>is </i>a definite errata here - Werewolf: the Forsaken says that a Wolf-Blooded who doesn't have a First Change keeps her Tell if she becomes a supernatural being. This directly conflicts with Awakening rules, which says that Tells go the way of the dodo post-Awakening.<br /> <br /> That should be clarified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T14:19:00-07:00","id":1319574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1319494-signs-of-sorcery-is-on-dtrpg?p=1319570#post1319570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This directly conflicts with Awakening rules, which says that Tells go the way of the dodo post-Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get why you'd think that, but I don't think it does. SoS specifies that you loose templates, supernatural merits and conditions/tilts. Tells aren't any of those, they're their own weird thing that specifically crosses templates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-19T14:33:00-07:00","id":1319576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1319494-signs-of-sorcery-is-on-dtrpg?p=1319574#post1319574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get why you'd think that, but I don't think it does. SoS specifies that you loose templates, supernatural merits and conditions/tilts. Tells aren't any of those, they're their own weird thing that specifically crosses templates.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty clear that they lose tells. &quot;Wolf-blooded can (though they lose their Wolf-Blooded Merits and tells when Awakening)&quot;<br /> <br /> I imagine it's so not every game is 'Mage and everyone's wolf-blooded,' since some of the Tells are incredibly useful, like seeing in all frequencies of Twilight or being able to cross the Gauntlet without using Supernal magic. I'd say it's a cynical thought, but there's already threads on how to get pack and lodge and Sacred Hunt bonuses as other splats entirely so it might come up